        "original_id": "eefaa2f6-9acb-5661-81f7-21d5675996ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Vanderbilt University, Bowdoin College, Kentucky Wesleyan College, Methodist Church, Kingswood College\n- People: Cornelius Vanderbilt, John Wesley Hughes\n- Places: Brunswick, Maine, Commonwealth of Massachusetts, Millersburg, Kentucky, Owensboro, Kentucky, Nashville, Tennessee, Kingswood, Kentucky\n- Topics: college founding, naming, endowments, education, pastoral service\n\nFacts:\n- Bowdoin College was chartered in 1794, when Maine was still part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\n- Vanderbilt University was founded in 1873 and was named in honor of Cornelius Vanderbilt.\n- Cornelius Vanderbilt provided Vanderbilt University with its initial $1 million endowment despite never having been to the South.\n- John Wesley Hughes attended Kentucky Wesleyan College in Millersburg, Kentucky, which is now located in Owensboro, Kentucky.\n- John Wesley Hughes served as a pastor in the Kentucky Conference of the Methodist Church before pursuing further education at Vanderbilt University in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- Kingswood College, founded by John Wesley Hughes, operated in Kingswood, Kentucky, from 1906 to 1934.\n- Bowdoin College is a private liberal arts college located in Brunswick, Maine.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6334087a-b0a4-5043-97aa-c284491bf33a",
        "text": "Page: Vanderbilt University. Sentence: Founded in 1873, it was named in honor of shipping and rail magnate Cornelius Vanderbilt, who provided the school its initial $1 million endowment despite having never been to the South.\nPage: Bowdoin College. Sentence: Bowdoin College ( ) is a private liberal arts college located in Brunswick, Maine.\nPage: Bowdoin College. Sentence: At the time Bowdoin was chartered in 1794, Maine was still a part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\nPage: John Wesley Hughes. Sentence: Hughes attended Kentucky Wesleyan College in Millersburg, Kentucky (now located in Owensboro, Kentucky), and served as a pastor in the Kentucky Conference of the Methodist Church before pursuing further education at Vanderbilt University in Nashville, Tennessee.\nPage: Kingswood, Kentucky. Sentence: Kingswood College founded by John Wesley Hughes operated in the community from 1906 to 1934.",
